The `dequeue` method first checks if the second stack is empty. If it is, it means that all items have been dequeued and the queue is empty. In this case, it returns `None`. Otherwise, it removes the last item from the second stack and returns it.

The `is_empty` method checks if both stacks are empty.

The `peek` method returns the last item in the second stack, which is the item that has been dequeued but not yet processed.

